> Alpha changes the geometry, not just the plotting colour

For each alpha, compute the grand centroid mu and labelled centroids mu_g
in the two retained coordinates. The external diagnostic is

\[
W=\sum_g\sum_{i\in g}\|z_i-\mu_g\|^2,\qquad
B=\sum_g n_g\|\mu_g-\mu\|^2,\qquad R=B/W.
\]

Expanding z_i-mu=(z_i-mu_g)+(mu_g-mu) makes the cross term vanish,
so total scatter is W+B. The ratio is invariant to translation, rotation,
sign flips and uniform nonzero scaling; it changes if the axes are scaled
differently. It is a descriptive ratio, not an F statistic or held-out
classification accuracy. The original same-data comparison selects alpha=0
for this particular two-coordinate separation score. It does not establish a
universally optimal density correction.

We retain the original direct maximum coordinate differences as a diagnostic,
but those depend on eigenvector sign and scale. Absolute Pearson correlation
of the first coordinates helps distinguish a sign flip from a different
ordering; separate eigenvalues and scatter ratios provide additional evidence.
No species labels are passed to any fit constructor. The larger axes at
alpha=1 reflect the D-weighted normalization, so compare structure as well
as axis magnitudes.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/diffusion_alpha.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");const auto iris=dm::datasets::iris();
  const std::vector<std::string> features{"Sepal.Length","Sepal.Width","Petal.Length","Petal.Width"};
  std::vector<std::string> labels;for(std::size_t i=0;i<iris.nrows();++i)labels.push_back(iris.string_at("Species",i));
  std::print("| alpha | between scatter | within scatter | between / within | lambda1 |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(double alpha:{0.,.5,1.}){
    const dm::stats::DiffusionMaps m(iris,features,{2,5.5,alpha,1});const auto r=dm::stats::embedding_separation(m.embedding(),labels);
    std::print("| {:.1f} | {:.6f} | {:.6f} | {:.4f} | {:.6f} |\n",alpha,r.between,r.within,r.ratio,m.eigenvalues()[1]);
  }
  const dm::stats::DiffusionMaps a(iris,features,{2,5.5,0,1}),b(iris,features,{2,5.5,1,1});
  std::print("\n| coordinate | raw max absolute difference | absolute Pearson correlation |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t c=0;c<2;++c){double difference=0;for(std::size_t i=0;i<iris.nrows();++i)difference=std::max(difference,std::abs(a.embedding()(i,c)-b.embedding()(i,c)));
    std::print("| {} | {:.4f} | {:.4f} |\n",c+1,difference,std::abs(dm::stats::pearson_correlation_test(a.dimension(c),b.dimension(c)).estimate1));}
  auto p=a.plot_embedding(labels),q=b.plot_embedding(labels);
  p.title("Alpha 0: original separation choice").x_label("diffusion coordinate 1").y_label("diffusion coordinate 2").y_limits(-.015,.03);
  q.title("Alpha 1: different degree correction").x_label("diffusion coordinate 1").y_label("diffusion coordinate 2").y_limits(-.8,.8);
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(p).add(q).size(1100,520).title("External labelled separation is exploratory, not held-out accuracy").fit_panels().save_svg("build/diffusion_alpha.svg");
}
