> The original Swiss roll and its known coordinates

The original program sampled 400 points with mt19937_64 seed 42,
interleaving two uniform draws per row:

\[
t=\frac{3\pi}{2}(1+2u),\quad h=21v,\quad
(x,y,z)=(t\cos t,h,t\sin t).
\]

The canonical generator now exposes that engine explicitly. Its default
three-argument Xoshiro generator remains unchanged; requesting Mt19937
reproduces the original report's draw sequence with libstdc++. Standard-library
uniform distribution mappings need not match across different C++ libraries.
All experiments below obtain the same generated frame through this API,
use x,y,z without scaling and keep t,height,arc_length outside the fit.

The angle parameter t is monotone along the spiral but is not distance along
it. Its flat coordinate is
s(t)=[t sqrt(1+t^2)+asinh(t)]/2, since the curve's speed is sqrt(1+t^2).
The unrolled sheet is a rectangle in (s,h), roughly 89 by 21. Uniform t does
not mean uniform arc length. We retain the original correlations with t
and also report correlations with s. Neither coordinate correlation alone
certifies a low-distortion two-dimensional recovery.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/diffusion_swiss_input.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto roll=dm::datasets::swiss_roll(400,0,42,dm::datasets::SwissRollEngine::Mt19937);
  const auto& x=roll.numeric_column("x").values();const auto& y=roll.numeric_column("y").values();const auto& z=roll.numeric_column("z").values();
  const auto& angle=roll.numeric_column("t").values();const auto& arc=roll.numeric_column("arc_length").values();
  const auto matrix=dm::linalg::DenseMatrix<double>::from_columns({x,y,z});
  const auto scales=dm::stats::manifold_distance_scales(matrix,8);const auto colors=dm::graphics::value_colors(angle);
  std::print("Swiss roll: {} rows; seed 42; mt19937_64; zero coordinate noise.\n\n",roll.nrows());
  std::print("| diagnostic in raw squared units | value |\n| :--- | ---: |\n| pairwise upper median | {:.4f} |\n| pairwise mean | {:.4f} |\n| eighth-neighbour upper median | {:.4f} |\n\n",scales.upper_median_squared,scales.mean_squared,scales.upper_median_neighbor_squared);
  std::print("First row: t={:.6f}, height={:.6f}, x={:.6f}, z={:.6f}.\n",angle[0],y[0],x[0],z[0]);
  auto p=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();p.points_colored(x,z,colors,4).title("Observed roll: top view").x_label("x = t cos(t)").y_label("z = t sin(t)");
  auto q=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();q.points_colored(arc,y,colors,4).title("Known flat sheet; withheld from fit").x_label("arc length s(t)").y_label("height h");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(p).add(q).size(1100,520).title("The same 400 points; colour runs from low t (purple) to high t (yellow)").fit_panels().save_svg("build/diffusion_swiss_input.svg");
}
```
